msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:34
#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:45
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:36
msgid ""
"Search for library in `PlatformIO Library Registry <https://platformio.org/"
"lib>`_ by :ref:`library_json` fields in the boolean mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:39
msgid "The boolean search capability supports the following operators:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:44
msgid "Operator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:46
msgid "``+``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:47
msgid ""
"A leading or trailing plus sign indicates that this word must be present in "
"library fields (see above) that is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:49
msgid "``-``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:50
msgid ""
"A leading or trailing minus sign indicates that this word must not be "
"present in any of the libraries that are returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:52
msgid "``(no operator)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:53
msgid ""
"By default (when neither ``+`` nor ``-`` is specified), the word is "
"optional, but the libraries that contain it are rated higher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:55
msgid "``> <``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:56
msgid ""
"These two operators are used to change a word's contribution to the "
"relevance value that is assigned to a library. The ``>`` operator increases "
"the contribution and the ``<`` operator decreases it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:59
msgid "``( )``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:60
msgid ""
"Parentheses group words into subexpressions. Parenthesized groups can be "
"nested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:62
msgid "``~``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:63
msgid ""
"A leading tilde acts as a negation operator, causing the word's contribution "
"to the library's relevance to be negative. This is useful for marking "
"\"noise\" words. A library containing such a word is rated lower than "
"others, but is not excluded altogether, as it would be with the ``-`` "
"operator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:67
msgid "``*``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:68
msgid ""
"The asterisk serves as the truncation (or wildcard) operator. Unlike the "
"other operators, it is appended to the word to be affected. Words match if "
"they begin with the word preceding the ``*`` operator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:71
msgid "``\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:72
msgid ""
"A phrase that is enclosed within double quote (``\"``) characters matches "
"only libraries that contain the phrase literally, as it was typed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:76
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/lib/cmd_search.rst:83
msgid "Filter libraries by registry ID"
msgstr ""

